   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to extending\nthe authority of the department of environmental conservation to manage deer\nand bear; and to amend chapter 600 of the laws of 1993, amending the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to the management of deer, in relation\nto the effectiveness of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S7047",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7047-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13, Chap 600 of 1993; amd §§11-0903 & 11-0913, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7047\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nextending the authority of the department of environmental conservation\nto manage deer and bear; and to amend chapter 600 of the laws of 1993,\namending the environmental conservation law relating to the management\nof deer, in relation to the effectiveness of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:  The purpose of this bill is to extend the\nauthority of the Department of Environmental Conservation (DEC) to\nmanage big game (white-tailed deer and black bear).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend Section 13 of Chapter 600 of the Laws\nof 1993 to extend, until December 31, 2024, the expiration date applica-\nble to several provisions of the Fish and Wildlife Law related to the\ntaking of deer.\n\nSection 2 of this bill would amend Environmental Conservation Law (ECL)\n§ 11-0903(8), (9)(a) and (10) to extend, until December 31, 2024, DEC's\nauthority to: I) regulate the taking of bear and the possession and\ndisposition of bear parts, and the intentional and incidental feeding of\nbears; 2) fix by regulation special open seasons for taking wild deer of\neither sex when in its opinion deer shall become numerous enough to\ncause substantial damage to property and overbrowsing; and 3) adopt\nregulations with respect to the manner of taking of, the possession of,\nand open seasons and bag limits for deer.\n\nSection 3 of this bill would amend ECL § 11-0913(1)(a) to extend until\nDecember 31, 2024, DEC's authority to issue Deer Management Permits.\n\nSection 4 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAuthority to set regulations for big game provides a timely administra-\ntive process which optimizes the effectiveness of harvest management\ntechniques. Each of the ECL provisions pertaining to management of black\nbear and deer is critical. Achieving management objectives for these\nspecies requires the ability to tailor seasons, bag limits, and other\nhunting regulations to reflect changing conditions for management units\nin the State. The ability to amend regulations provides the flexibility\nneeded to respond to these needs on a timely basis. In the absence of\nthese renewed authorities, DEC's deer and bear management programs would\nrevert to the \"default\" statutes, thereby instituting archaic and inef-\nfective big game management regimes. PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  DEC's\nregulatory authority for dear and bear was last extended by Chapter 383\nof the Laws of 2018.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
